cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Luxar, please cite it as below."
title: "Luxar: Gaussian splatting and interactive web visualization for multidimensional scientific data"
abstract: >-
  Luxar is an open-source, Python-first system that compiles arbitrary
  n-dimensional scientific data — points, lines, and Gaussian splats — into
  compact, spatially indexed Zarr archives served to a browser-based WebGL
  viewer with HDR rendering, progressive streaming, and native n-dimensional
  navigation. It includes a pipeline for fitting microscopy volumes to Gaussian
  splats as a compact, continuous, GPU-renderable representation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Royer
    given-names: "Loïc A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9991-9724"
    affiliation: "Chan Zuckerberg Biohub, San Francisco"
    email: loic.royer@czbiohub.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/royerlab/luxar"
url: "https://github.com/royerlab/luxar"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - scientific-visualization
  - gaussian-splatting
  - microscopy
  - n-dimensional
  - webgl
  - zarr
